# File Index Monitor Skill

## Purpose
This skill monitors the QMD file index for staleness and scheduling compliance.

## Capabilities
- Verify index freshness against source file modification times
- Check if scheduled scans are running within acceptable intervals
- Report outdated files and missed scans
- Generate audit reports in both human-readable and machine-readable formats

## Implementation
```typescript
// Load the index manifest
const indexManifest = fs.readFileSync('.index/qmd_manifest.json', 'utf8');
const index = JSON.parse(indexManifest);

// Load cron configuration
const cronConfig = fs.readFileSync('config/cron_monitor.json', 'utf8');
const cron = JSON.parse(cronConfig);

// Current timestamp
const now = Date.now();

// Generate findings
const findings = [];

// Check each file for staleness
index.files.forEach(file => {
  const modTime = new Date(file.modifiedTime).getTime();
  const indexedTime = new Date(file.indexedAt).getTime();
  const sinceIndexed = now - indexedTime;
  const stalenessThreshold = 30 * 60 * 1000; // 30 minutes in ms

  if (modTime > indexedTime && sinceIndexed > stalenessThreshold) {
    findings.push({
      issue_type: 'file_stale',
      evidence_file: file.path,
      finding: `File modified ${Math.floor((modTime - indexedTime) / 60000)} minutes before current scan`,
      recommendation: 'Run incremental index update or manually update affected content'
    });
  }
});

// Check scan timing
const qmdIndexJob = cron.jobs.find(j => j.name === 'qmd_index_incremental');
const lastQmdScan = new Date(qmdIndexJob.lastRunTimestamp).getTime();
const sinceLastScan = now - lastQmdScan;
const maxInterval = qmdIndexJob.intervalMinutes * 60 * 1000;
const alertThreshold = cron.alertThresholdMinutes * 60 * 1000;

if (sinceLastScan > maxInterval) {
  findings.push({
    issue_type: 'scan_delayed',
    evidence_file: 'config/cron_monitor.json',
    finding: `qmd_index_incremental scan last ran ${Math.floor(sinceLastScan / 60000)} minutes ago (max allowed: ${qmdIndexJob.intervalMinutes} minutes)`,
    recommendation: 'Investigate why scans are not running on schedule; check crontab or scheduler status'
  });
}

// Generate report
generateAuditReport(findings);
```

## Usage
1. Run this skill after making changes to QMD files
2. Review the generated audit report
3. Address any findings before proceeding with analysis

## Output Files
- `reports/index-audit.md`: Human-readable audit report
- `reports/audit-findings.json`: Machine-readable JSON with all findings
